{"authored" [{"question" "q-104058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine whether a differentiable classical solution on an open interval containing the initial point exists for the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/review.json" "file_sha256" "3d30be9571d956cd2bc36f1f54b2d34833a0266bc8ce5b5b3096383861573c7f" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "d927700eb35f081d13e34645350f7a17edc608fee7e1381d32f15ccd77544465" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/verification.json" "basis" 2238 "rationale" "The initial point makes the original differential equation require 0*yprime(1)=2. Retain its equation and initial data, clarify classical existence, replace the erroneous solution and add the correct no-solution choice with a new field version while preserving all source fields, answers, IDs and history."} {"question" "q-104058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A classical solution must be differentiable on an interval containing $x=1$ and satisfy the differential equation at that point. Substituting $x=1$ and $y(1)=1$ gives\n\n$$\\left(\\frac{1}{1\\cdot1}-\\frac11\\right)y'(1)=2,\\qquad 0\\cdot y'(1)=2.$$\n\nThis is impossible for a finite derivative. Therefore no differentiable classical solution exists for the stated initial condition.\n\nFormal separation on nonsingular regions gives\n\n$$(1/y-1)\\,dy=2x\\,dx,\\qquad \\ln|y|-y=x^2+C.$$\n\nRequiring the integrated level set to contain $(1,1)$ yields $C=-2$, hence $\\ln|y|-y=x^2-2$. This is the source's formally integrated relation, but it is not a classical solution of the IVP. Differentiating it at $(1,1)$ again requires $0\\cdot y'(1)=2$. Near $y=1$, continuity would give $y>0$, and $\\ln y-y\\le -1$ makes $x^2\\le1$ necessary on that level set, so it cannot supply a graph on a two-sided neighborhood of $x=1$ either.\n\nThe source capture and its accepted formal relation are retained for provenance. The corrected study answer concerns the original IVP's existence." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/review.json" "file_sha256" "3d30be9571d956cd2bc36f1f54b2d34833a0266bc8ce5b5b3096383861573c7f" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "d927700eb35f081d13e34645350f7a17edc608fee7e1381d32f15ccd77544465" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/verification.json" "basis" 2238 "rationale" "The initial point makes the original differential equation require 0*yprime(1)=2. Retain its equation and initial data, clarify classical existence, replace the erroneous solution and add the correct no-solution choice with a new field version while preserving all source fields, answers, IDs and history."} {"question" "q-104058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No differentiable classical solution exists."] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/review.json" "file_sha256" "3d30be9571d956cd2bc36f1f54b2d34833a0266bc8ce5b5b3096383861573c7f" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "d927700eb35f081d13e34645350f7a17edc608fee7e1381d32f15ccd77544465" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-104058/verification.json" "basis" 2238 "rationale" "The initial point makes the original differential equation require 0*yprime(1)=2. Retain its equation and initial data, clarify classical existence, replace the erroneous solution and add the correct no-solution choice with a new field version while preserving all source fields, answers, IDs and history."} {"question" "q-104058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e21cf1956a44dd6311069eef0655aae07e65cb301654ea6ee1e1dc82182b0d78" "basis" 2237 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|-1 & ={1}^{2}+C \\\\ 0-1 & =1+C \\\\ C & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ in implicit form is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e21cf1956a44dd6311069eef0655aae07e65cb301654ea6ee1e1dc82182b0d78" "basis" 2237 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c097b443fe834d701881765ef06b2ccca34858447fd15a076ba25dbfa4614f6" "basis" 2237 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-104058" []} "basis" 2238 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186354862 17592186354863 17592186354864 17592186354865 17592186354866 17592186354875] "immutable_fields" [[17592186354874 :answer-field/correct] [17592186354874 :answer-field/id] [17592186354874 :answer-field/key] [17592186354874 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
